    "result_text": "The build is green. Only one test class exists in this project (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement in `ClinicServiceImpl`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java:63`), mirroring the existing `AUDIT` logger convention.\n\n2. **Emitted the welcome notification on successful create** \u2014 inside the `saveOwner` `creating` block, after the owner is persisted (so `owner.getId()` and `owner.getMemberId()` are populated):\n\n```java\nNOTIFY.info(\"welcome notification enqueued: ownerId={} memberId={}\",\n    owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n```\n\nThe line is emitted only on create (guarded by the existing `creating` flag), and carries both the owner id and the memberId, satisfying the test's `notify.anyContains(String.valueOf(id), memberId)` assertion.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
